# Conformance probe pack for gate blocks (spec 0.17, Encode step 3): a gate
# one of whose bits a raw key writes. Fixed `bits` layout, least significant
# bit first. Public. No kinds. One byte per word. Exercises: a gate any of
# whose bits is written gets no value and is evaluated on the bits as they
# are, so a present c1 leaves the gate at 0 or 1 and qty cannot be encoded;
# without c1 the gate gets its value 3.
#
#   byte 0       bits 0-1: qty is valid when both are 1; bit 0 is also c1
#   byte 1       qty
format     conformance-gates-partial
version    0.17.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
field   probe.c1   0:0:1   uint
if      0:0:2  3
  field probe.qty  0:8:8   uint
end
